I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md, but it isn't committed: session_plan/ is gitignored, so the plain git add from the instructions failed and the || true swallowed it. I force-added and committed it at first, then soft-reset that unpushed commit so the ignored file wouldn't end up tracked. HEAD is still 0d37d01f and the file is on disk for the planner.

Build and probes: The harness reported a green build and test run; I didn't re-run the suite. The binary matches HEAD, and yoyo -p "say ok" returned Ok with exit 0. Probes from an empty folder outside git confirmed three open bugs on today's binary:
• #1091: yoyo grep hello a b searches one path called a b and exits 2.
• #1086: bare yoyo find prints usage: /find, the REPL syntax, on the shell.
• #1088: yoyo watch "echo a" prints "Watch mode ON" and exits 0, but the setting dies with the process.

New, not filed yet: yoyo refs hello goes to the model as a prompt and costs an API call, while its sibling yoyo def has its own shell command. Shell --help lists def as a subcommand but shows refs only in the REPL section.

Recent runs: the four completed evolve runs all succeeded, there were no reverts in 14 days, and the CI failures in the window are 8 days old and green since. The trajectory flags that 5 of the last 10 self-driven changes were in the prompt code, so this session's own pick should go somewhere else.

Competitors:
• Same fixes as ours: Claude Code 2.1.311 (released Oct 26) shipped two fixes that match what we did independently today: escaping hidden characters in JSON output (our #1092) and showing a timed-out command's output so far.
• Same hazard as #1057: it also fixed a background worker's worktree being removed while the worker was still running, which is the same hazard as our open #1057.
• Bash description: it corrected a bash tool description that wrongly claimed the working directory carries over between calls. Ours says nothing either way, and I confirmed cd does not carry over in yoyo.
• Codex 0.164: it hides credentials from bash commands, which bears on #1064. Its bundled default model is now GPT-6.1 Sol, which bears on #1037.

I saved these findings to yopedia.

Suggested priorities:
1. #1091, which is small, measured, and already has the reference grep behaviour on the ticket.
2. #1086 together with its sibling #1083.
3. #1088.
4. #1057.
5. A one-line bash description fix saying cd and export don't carry over.

#1078 and #1071 need the owner because they touch protected files. #1089, a community request for outreach on X, needs a reply naming who decides about public identity, not code.
